{"id":"b13","n":13,"title_ko":"Epiphany","title_en":"Epiphany","album":"Love Yourself 結 Answer","year":2018,"yt":"fIkZOLsnoqY","hook":[8,9,10,11,12],"notes":{"s":"Jin's solo: the person he was supposed to love turns out to be himself.","t":"Jin's solo and the comeback trailer for Love Yourself 結 Answer, August 2018, a straight rock ballad that lands the 結 resolution. Heard against the other three solos it works as a reply: Euphoria made someone else the cause and Serendipity made someone else the rescue, and this one withdraws the question from them. The series finishes its argument on Answer: Love Myself, but fans point here as the place the turn actually happens, because the self-erasure gets named first and refused second rather than skipped. It is also the track most often cited for the vocal rather than the concept.","k":[["뭐든 너에게 맞추고","맞추다 is tuning one thing to another, the verb for setting a watch or adjusting seasoning. The line is not I pleased you; it is I reset my own settings to yours. That is why what follows treats it as a loss of shape rather than as an act of kindness, and why the storm is in his own chest."],["웃고 있는 가면","가면 is a theatrical or carnival mask, and 가면을 쓰다 is the ordinary idiom for concealing your real self. The smiling-mask image runs straight into the persona thread the group built an entire later album around, so this is the hinge between Love Yourself and Map of the Soul."],["이제야 깨달아","이제 is now, and the -야 particle adds not until. So the line carries a reproach at himself for how late the realisation is, which plain now I realise throws away. One particle is holding the emotional weight of the chorus."],["너무 아름다운 걸, 내가 곧 나인 걸","-ㄴ 걸 contracts -ㄴ 것을 and works as a sentence ending for something just understood and half announced to yourself. It is why the chorus sounds like a discovery rather than a declaration, and it is everywhere in Korean ballads once you can hear it."]]},"vocab":[{"w":"이상하다","en":"strange, odd, wrong","i":0},{"w":"맞추다","en":"to fit, adjust, tune to","note":"시계를 맞추다 set a watch, 간을 맞추다 season to taste; the object is what gets adapted","i":2},{"w":"폭풍","en":"storm, tempest","i":5},{"w":"감당하다","en":"to handle, bear, cope with","note":"Usually of a burden that may exceed you, so 감당할 수 없다 is very common","i":5},{"w":"가면","en":"mask","note":"가면을 쓰다 is the idiom for hiding your true self","i":6},{"w":"모습","en":"appearance, form, the way one is","note":"Wider than face or looks; 내 모습 is nearer to who I am","i":7},{"w":"드러내다","en":"to reveal, expose, show","note":"Transitive; 드러나다 is for something coming to light on its own","i":7},{"w":"빛나다","en":"to shine, glow","i":9},{"w":"소중하다","en":"precious, dear, to be treasured","i":9},{"w":"영혼","en":"soul, spirit","i":9},{"w":"깨닫다","en":"to realise, come to understand","note":"ㄷ-irregular, so the ㄷ becomes ㄹ before a vowel and gives 깨달아","i":10},{"w":"부족하다","en":"lacking, insufficient, not enough","note":"Of supplies and of people; used about yourself it is modest rather than harsh","i":11},{"w":"아름답다","en":"beautiful","note":"ㅂ-irregular, giving 아름다운 and 아름다워","i":11},{"w":"숨기다","en":"to hide something","note":"Causative of 숨다, to hide oneself","i":14},{"w":"두렵다","en":"to fear, dread","i":15},{"w":"뭉툭하다","en":"blunt, stubby","note":"Of a pencil tip or a nose; the opposite of 날카롭다","i":22},{"w":"수줍다","en":"shy, bashful","i":23},{"w":"광채","en":"brilliance, radiance","i":23},{"w":"따위","en":"that sort of thing, the likes of","note":"Dismissive. Aimed at a person it is rude, so it is usually aimed at a thing","i":23},{"w":"지금껏","en":"up to now, all this time","note":"-껏 attaches to time words meaning as far as, also 여태껏 and 아직껏","i":25}],"items":[{"i":0,"ko":"참 이상해","r":"cham isanghae","tk":[{"s":"참","r":"cham","m":[{"t":"참","p":"NNG","pl":"noun","en":["really, truly"]}]},{"s":"이상해","r":"isanghae","m":[{"t":"이상해","p":"NNG","l":"이상하다","pl":"verb","en":["strange, odd, wrong"]}]}],"en":"It's so strange"},{"i":1,"ko":"분명 나 너를 너무 사랑했는데","r":"bunmy